@startuml
title lowes/auditor — System Architecture (Component View)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam arrowFontSize 11

package "JVM 11 Application Environment" {

  component "Integrating Application" as App

  rectangle "AuditorEventConfig" as Config <<data>> {
    note as ConfigNote
      applicationName
      eventSource
      eventSubType
      metadata
      filters.element {
        enabled,
        types,
        includes
      }
    end note
  }

  package "lowes/auditor (Kotlin Client Library)" {

    component "Auditing API" as AuditAPI
    component "Audit Comparison Engine" as DiffEngine
    component "AuditEvent Builder" as EventBuilder

    interface "EventPublisher" as EventPublisherI
    interface "LogProvider" as LogProviderI
    interface "AuditEventElementFilter" as ElementFilterI
  }

  rectangle "AuditEvent" as AuditEvent <<data>> {
    note as AuditEventNote
      type: UPDATED | CREATED | DELETED
      elements[]:
        name
        updatedValue
        previousValue
        metadata.fqdn
      published as JSON string
    end note
  }

  component "Kafka Event Publisher\n(default implementation)" as KafkaPublisher
  component "InclusionFilter" as InclusionFilter

  component "Kafka Topic" as KafkaTopic

  component "Downstream Consumer\n(out of scope)" as Consumer
}

App --> AuditAPI : oldObject, newObject,\nAuditorEventConfig
App --> Config : supplies configuration
AuditAPI --> Config : reads

AuditAPI --> DiffEngine : compare old vs new state
DiffEngine --> ElementFilterI : apply element filtering
ElementFilterI <|.. InclusionFilter

DiffEngine --> EventBuilder : changed elements\n(UPDATED / CREATED / DELETED)
EventBuilder --> AuditEvent : creates
Config ..> EventBuilder : configuration values

EventBuilder --> EventPublisherI : publish(AuditEvent JSON)
EventPublisherI <|.. KafkaPublisher
KafkaPublisher --> KafkaTopic : serialized AuditEvent

KafkaTopic --> Consumer : AuditEvent JSON

EventBuilder ..> LogProviderI : logging support
AuditAPI ..> LogProviderI : logging support

note right of ElementFilterI
  NFR-001 / C-001 / C-004:
  abstract integration point
  for element filtering
end note

note bottom of KafkaPublisher
  C-003: default transport is Kafka,
  abstracted behind EventPublisher
end note

@enduml
